WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.541 --> 00:00:17.103
waited in front of a huge stone gate while his parents bought tickets for a tour of Alnwick

2
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:23.587
Castle. He had been looking forward to seeing the medieval castle where scenes from the Harry Potter movies

3
00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:24.247
had been filmed.

4
00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:30.010
The ancient stone castle looked impressive, but Tyler felt disappointed.

5
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.744
"This doesn't look like Hogwarts," he thought.

6
00:00:35.165 --> 00:00:38.526
Hogwarts was the name of Harry Potter's awesome-looking wizard school.

7
00:00:38.546 --> 00:00:45.749
"Hello!" A woman suddenly appeared in front of him, dressed in a robe just like a student from

8
00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:49.331
Hogwarts. She looked oddly familiar.

9
00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:51.772
The woman grinned.

10
00:00:51.792 --> 00:00:56.234
"Potter fans always expect to see Hogwarts when they arrive.

11
00:00:57.374 --> 00:01:01.836
But most of what you see on-screen is really a model or special effects.

12
00:01:04.556 --> 00:01:08.640
Don't be too disappointed though—Alnwick has plenty of magic.

13
00:01:09.981 --> 00:01:12.283
I'm Edwina, and I'll show you around."

14
00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:20.190
Edwina waved a wand, and fog filled the air.

15
00:01:21.491 --> 00:01:27.056
When it cleared, Tyler was surrounded by people dressed in medieval clothing, and the castle's stone walls were

16
00:01:27.096 --> 00:01:27.996
now made of wood!

17
00:01:29.558 --> 00:01:30.819
"Where are we?"

18
00:01:31.199 --> 00:01:31.860
Tyler murmured.

19
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.201
"Alnwick Castle," Edwina said.

20
00:01:35.221 --> 00:01:42.484
"We're touring the castle during the eleventh century, when castles were built of wood, not stone.

21
00:01:44.885 --> 00:01:50.948
Castle-builders constructed the main building of a castle on top of a hill and enclosed the castle grounds

22
00:01:50.988 --> 00:01:52.709
with a large wooden wall."

23
00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.830
Tyler wrinkled his nose.

24
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.952
"Did wood offer much protection?"

25
00:02:00.568 --> 00:02:02.890
"Wooden castles were actually strong.

26
00:02:04.151 --> 00:02:10.656
But for even more protection, builders dug ditches called moats around the hill and outside the walls.

27
00:02:11.757 --> 00:02:13.718
The moats were often filled with water."

28
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.424
Tyler looked around the lively yard where blacksmiths were hammering weapons, and servants were milling wheat.

29
00:02:22.665 --> 00:02:26.688
Suddenly a loud horn blasted, and a drawbridge was yanked up.

30
00:02:28.052 --> 00:02:31.255
Then soldiers with bows and arrows ran along the walls.

31
00:02:31.275 --> 00:02:33.697
"What's going on?"

32
00:02:33.977 --> 00:02:34.657
Tyler cried.

33
00:02:34.677 --> 00:02:37.159
"An attack," Edwina said.

34
00:02:37.179 --> 00:02:43.845
"In the early part of the medieval period, nobles had more power than their monarchs and ruled their

35
00:02:43.905 --> 00:02:45.126
lands from their castles.

36
00:02:46.727 --> 00:02:52.732
Nobles were often at war with each other, or their monarchs, and battles were frequent—and violent.

37
00:02:54.213 --> 00:02:56.115
But don't worry—we're about to leave."

38
00:02:57.768 --> 00:03:00.949
She waved her wand again, and Tyler heaved a sigh of relief.

39
00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.791
The wooden wall had turned back to stone, and the soldiers were gone.

40
00:03:08.052 --> 00:03:13.355
The castle yard was still full of activity, but now a large stone building stood on the hill.

41
00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:18.737
"Come on," Edwina said, "let's go see inside.

42
00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:23.339
As time went on, castles evolved," she explained.

43
00:03:23.359 --> 00:03:29.013
"By the twelfth century, castle-builders were mainly using stone.

44
00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:34.254
Here, in the fourteenth century, Alnwick took its present shape.

45
00:03:35.535 --> 00:03:42.777
Castles became important social centers under the feudal system, which was the way that society was organized during

46
00:03:42.817 --> 00:03:43.917
the medieval period.

47
00:03:45.318 --> 00:03:51.159
Monarchs had more power now, but they shared it with nobles in exchange for support and military service.

48
00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.863
Nobles, in turn, let peasants live on their land in exchange for taxes and military service.

49
00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:04.369
Castles also provided protection for the surrounding community in times of war."

50
00:04:07.091 --> 00:04:09.133
Tyler followed Edwina inside the building.

51
00:04:10.274 --> 00:04:13.136
It was dark and stony, just like the castle's exterior.

52
00:04:13.156 --> 00:04:18.600
"Eventually nobles lost power as monarchs developed central governments.

53
00:04:21.343 --> 00:04:26.637
Wars became less frequent, and castles were no longer vital for a kingdom's defenses.

54
00:04:28.278 --> 00:04:32.039
England's feudal system officially ended in 1660.

55
00:04:33.679 --> 00:04:40.341
Many castles in the British Isles were abandoned or torn down, but some, like Alnwick, continued to be

56
00:04:40.481 --> 00:04:45.882
occupied." Edwina flicked her wand, and the castle transformed again.

57
00:04:47.783 --> 00:04:50.844
Tyler gasped at the marble walls and crystal chandeliers.

58
00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.061
"Only the rich could afford to live in a castle," Edwina said.

59
00:04:56.081 --> 00:05:03.883
"But even though castle owners installed running water, gas, and electricity, living in a castle wasn't easy.

60
00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:12.686
Maintaining such old, large buildings was expensive, so many families gave up their castles in the twentieth century.

61
00:05:13.826 --> 00:05:18.928
Some castles found other uses and became hospitals, prisons, or museums.

62
00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.082
Alnwick was used by schools and colleges."

63
00:05:24.843 --> 00:05:28.385
Tyler followed Edwina outdoors along a path that led toward the gate.

64
00:05:28.405 --> 00:05:33.288
"Today Alnwick is still a private home," she said.

65
00:05:33.308 --> 00:05:42.574
"As an intact medieval castle, it's also a tourist attraction and popular filming location."

66
00:05:43.654 --> 00:05:46.296
She stopped and gestured toward a large grassy area.

67
00:05:48.064 --> 00:05:51.608
"This is where we filmed a broom-flying lesson scene."

68
00:05:51.628 --> 00:05:55.271
"We?" Tyler repeated, confused.

69
00:05:56.352 --> 00:06:02.658
Just then it hit him Edwina laughed at his startled expression.

70
00:06:02.678 --> 00:06:06.882
"I was an extra in one of the Harry Potter movies!"

71
00:06:08.304 --> 00:06:10.226
"That's why you look familiar!"

72
00:06:11.687 --> 00:06:12.368
Edwina nodded.

73
00:06:13.368 --> 00:06:18.731
"Production companies often hire local people as extras, and I was one of them."

74
00:06:20.052 --> 00:06:23.014
With a smile, she flicked the wand again—and disappeared!

75
00:06:24.314 --> 00:06:25.035
Tyler blinked.

76
00:06:25.055 --> 00:06:28.016
"What just happened?"

77
00:06:28.477 --> 00:06:29.637
he thought, shaking his head.

78
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.200
We got the tickets!"

79
00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.101
Mom called, waving him over.

80
00:06:40.103 --> 00:06:41.244
Dad scratched his head.

81
00:06:42.492 --> 00:06:44.573
"Are you sure this is the right castle?

82
00:06:44.814 --> 00:06:46.394
It doesn't look like Hogwarts."

83
00:06:48.276 --> 00:06:49.016
Tyler smiled.

84
00:06:49.036 --> 00:06:52.278
"The filmmakers used lots of special effects.

85
00:06:52.838 --> 00:06:57.241
But don't worry, Dad, I've been uh, looking around.

86
00:06:58.361 --> 00:07:00.483
And the castle is definitely magical.

87
00:07:00.803 --> 00:07:01.403
Let's go see it!"
